cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  agent-harness-anatomy: findings from building and dismantling an
  autonomous ML-research pipeline
message: "If you refer to these findings, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yun"
    given-names: "Yunsu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BluePinetree/agent-harness-anatomy"
abstract: >-
  A study record of an autonomous machine-learning research pipeline built on a
  multi-agent LLM framework and run 271 times. Documents four findings: that the
  framework was wrapping a single agent while coordination was hand-written; that
  numbers produced by LLM-authored code cannot be adjudicated on and a fixed code
  layer must own the evidence; seven measured failure modes in which the system
  reported success it could not substantiate; and the engineering required to keep
  multi-hour runs alive, which short-horizon agent benchmarks do not exercise.
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - agent-harness
  - multi-agent-systems
  - research-automation
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
